Aggregate functions
________ _________

count(): count the number of records.
sum(): returns the total sum of numeric column.
avg(): return the average value.
min(): returns the minimum value.
max(): returns the maximum value.

CLAUSES
_______

In MySQL clauses are used to control how data is selected , filtered , grouped , sorted, or modified in SQL
queries.

Think of clauses like instructions given to the database.

1. Where clause:
________________

filter records based on specific condition where claus can be used as comparision operators ,logical 
operators..etc operators.

syntax:
select column1,column2,.....
from table
where condition.

Group by clause:
_______________

the group by clause is used to group rows having the same values in one or more columns. It is only commonly 
used with aggregate functions such as sum(),min()<max(),avg(),count().

syntax:
_______

select column-name,aggregate_function(column-name)
from table
group by column_name;

Having clause:
_____________

the having clause is used to filter grouped records after group by clause. 
it is similar to where but it works on grouped instead o findividual rows.

syntax:
______

select column-name, aggregate_function (column_name)
from table
group by column_name
having condition;

Order by:
_____ __

the order by clause is used to sort the result set in ascending order (ASC) or descending order(DESC)

ASC--> ascending order by default
DESC--> descending order

syntax: 
______

select column-name
from table-name
order by column-name;

